From 0134498c3dbc8f929a6ea877958e9ddb7bc6f586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MR. ARX" <dev@nexeris.dev>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:23:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Perf: cut serial round-trips on the video page and every
 TopNav render

Three independent fixes, all measured from a real read of the request
waterfall, not guesswork:

1. app/learn/video/[id]/page.tsx was doing up to 5 SEQUENTIAL Supabase
   queries (video -> parentBoard -> siblingBoards -> siblingVideos ->
   recommended), each one waiting on the last. parentBoard, siblingBoards,
   and siblingVideos don't depend on each other -- they now run in one
   Promise.all wave. Only 'recommended' still has to wait (it needs
   siblingBoards' ids). 5 waterfall steps -> 3.

2. TopNav was fetching the Google avatar/name client-side on every mount
   (a full extra round trip AFTER the page already loaded, plus a visible
   avatar pop-in) even though getAuth() already has that exact data in
   hand server-side (Supabase's user.user_metadata, from the same
   supabase.auth.getUser() call getAuth() already makes). AuthResult's
   AUTHORIZED variant now carries a profile field; every TopNav call
   site passes auth.profile straight through. Removed the client effect
   entirely.

3. The video page's iframe used to always wait for a client-side POST to
   /api/video/[id]/play (fired from useEffect, after hydration) before
   it could even start loading. buildBunnyEmbedUrl moved to lib/bunny.ts
   (shared, was route-local) so the video page can build the exact same
   URL server-side, in the same query wave as the rest of the page's
   data, and hand it to VideoPlayer as an initial value. The heartbeat
   that re-verifies access every 4 minutes is completely unchanged --
   this only shortcuts the very first load. Logs the same
   VIDEO_ACCESS_GRANTED audit event the route would have, for parity.

Net effect on the video page specifically (the most-visited page): was
auth -> 5 sequential DB queries -> render -> hydrate -> fetch avatar ->
fetch playback URL -> iframe finally starts loading. Now: auth -> 3
query waves -> render, with iframe src and avatar both already correct
on first paint. No behavior change, no new data exposed to the client
that wasn't already reaching it (the embed URL and profile data were
always sent to the browser eventually -- this just stops making the
browser wait on a follow-up round trip to get the same thing a moment
later).
